  "race_position": "Option B of a 4-way derivation race for Δ_λ(K).  Option B = Frobenius co-Casimir restriction (theorem-forced, vortex-blind, 0 free parameters).  Other options under separate PRs.",
  "interpretation": "Δ_λ^B is FORCED by thm:frobenius-codim-universal — there is no freedom to fit it.  If the residual is small (≪ 0.1 MeV), co-Casimir restriction is the categorical Δ_λ selector and the deuteron binding ≈ -2.225 MeV is reproduced from the structure of C_dim_q alone, without any per-vortex tuning. If the residual is large (≥ 1 MeV), this option fails — the Frobenius co-Casimir is vortex-blind (per the .md theorem section 'Independence of the vortex'), so it cannot encode vortex-specific binding by itself; some additional vortex-dependent piece (Option A / C / D in the race) must carry it.",
  "honest_reporting_note": "Δ_λ^B is fixed at 1/dim_q(λ) by theorem — NOT rescaled to match M(D).  The diagnostic_closure_rescaler field reports what uniform rescaling would close the equation, but that rescaling is NOT applied to Δ_λ in the reported per_lambda table.  The reported residual is the un-tuned, theorem-only result.  Field renamed from `diagnostic_lambda_scale` per PR #1080 framing (no λ_scale; the framework's per-knot factor is VolDensity).",
  "follow_up": "If Option B residual is small for D, extend to (T, ³He) at n=9 (p(9)=30) and ⁴He at n=12 (p(12)=77) — the per-isotypic 1/dim_q profile is universal across all H_n(q), so the only atom-dependence is via y_λ(q_0) and χ^λ(β_K).  If Option B residual is large for D, document the gap and let the race favour another option (A: Plancherel truncation; C: jet-knot cohomology; D: minimum-norm pseudoinverse)."
